00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:17.784
in Paris right now and

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:20.387
looks like their clashes are erupting

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:21.321
once again.

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:23.089
Taking a live look. Look, May Day.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:24.357
May 1st is a day

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.693
treated as a holiday in many countries

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.128
to support

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.463
to a sorry.

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:30.830
The controller

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:31.564
and speaking to

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:33.900
Mayday is often celebrated

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:35.735
with demonstrations

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:38.738
as a holiday to recognize labor rights.

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:41.307
It is hitting differently this time.

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:42.842
This May 1st in Paris

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:45.211
because this is coming against continued

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.247
kind of outrage and controversy

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:48.114
over French

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:50.450
President Macron's move to reform

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.619
and overhaul the pension system there,

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:53.953
which also included

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:56.389
raising the retirement age by two years.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.291
Melissa Bell is on the street

00:00:58.291 --> 00:00:59.726
for us in Paris.

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:00.493
She's joining us now,

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:01.461
